# Task
Build a single, self-contained HTML file (inline CSS + tiny JS) that implements a 3-screen UI with smooth CSS transitions. Keep the code clean and production-ready. Use GPU-friendly transforms and respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Reuse existing UI classes; do NOT invent new button/input styles.

## Screens & States
- Three sections: **Screen 1**, **Screen 2**, **Screen 3**.
- App states via root attribute: `.app[data-state="intro"|"normal"|"menu-open"]`.
- Initial load (`intro`): only Screen 1 is visible full-screen; Screens 2/3 are off-canvas right.
- On **Start**: Screen 1 shrinks/morphs into a **circular chip** (top-left, fixed), 75px x 75px, app state → `normal`; Screens 2 & 3 slide/scale in from the right and take their normal positions (Screen 2 top, Screen 3 bottom). logo.svg stays visible in circle, rest of content invisible.
- In `normal`: clicking the top-left circle toggles `menu-open` and expands Screen 1 from the circle into a **panel** (no separate modal).
- In `menu-open`: Screens 2/3 remain visible to the right (slightly dimmed). Clicking outside or the circle closes back to `normal`.

## Screen 1 specifics
- The **circle** displays a centered **inline SVG logo** (no raster images).
- When opened (`menu-open`), Screen 1 becomes a left-docked panel with **width = 50vw (max 720px)** on desktop, **92vw** on mobile; anchored top-left; rounded corners; `overflow:hidden`.
- Inside this panel:
  1) **Nav tiles row** (large image tiles as links) at the top.
  2) **Settings** below, implemented as **ARIA tabs**:
     - Tabs: Appearance, Account (Clerk mount), Usage (Minutes Left), Subscription (Subscribe Now), About (links: Website, About, SenDev, Imprint).
     - Use proper ARIA roles (`tablist`/`tab`/`tabpanel`) and keyboard support (←/→, Home/End). Only selected panel is visible.

## Strict component reuse
Use existing classes only for UI elements:
- Buttons: `.btn`, `.btn--primary`, `.btn--secondary`, `.btn--sm`, `.btn--lg`
- Inputs/selectors/toggles: `.input`, `.select`, `.toggle`
- Form layout: `.field`, `.field__label`, `.field__control`
- Info chips: `.chip`, `.chip--accent`
Do **not** redefine these; only compose layout and write animation styles around them.

## Layout (high level)
- Desktop: Screen 2 (top ~60% height) + Screen 3 (bottom ~40%) within main area to the right of Screen 1 panel when open.
- Mobile: Screens 2/3 stack vertically; when menu open, they subtly scale/slide back to indicate background context.
- Circle size: ~72px mobile, ~96px desktop. Z-index: circle/logo > Screen1 panel > Screens 2&3.

## Animations (high level)
- Use transitions on transform/opacity/border-radius/clip-path. No animating `left/top` if avoidable.
- Circle ↔ Panel: scale/morph with `transform-origin: top left`.
- Screens 2/3 enter from right with small scale+opacity.
- Tabs: fade/slide for panel content; instant swap when reduced motion is on.

## Accessibility
- The circle is a button with `aria-expanded`.
- Tabs follow WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices. Focus management: move focus into selected tabpanel on open; return to circle on close.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.

## Minimal JS
- Toggle root `data-state` (`intro` → `normal` on Start; `normal` ↔ `menu-open` on circle/backdrop).
- Manage `aria-expanded` on the circle.
- Tabs: update `aria-selected`, `tabindex`, and show/hide panels; handle keyboard navigation.

## Deliverable
Output a single HTML file with:
- `<style>` containing all layout and animation CSS (variables for durations/easings/sizes).
- `<script>` with minimal state toggles and tab logic (no frameworks).
- Minimal semantic markup for Screen 2/3 placeholders.
- A small inline SVG logo placeholder in the circle.

